PURPOSE

H147 established three useful facts.

1.

LOCAL PATCHING
IS CHEAP
AND EFFECTIVE

inside:
a genuinely local repair regime.

2.

SPATIAL DIFFUSION
IS A REAL
MODE-SWITCH SIGNAL.

LOCAL-10:

blastema:
8%.

DIFFUSE-10:

blastema:
100%.

3.

The frozen H147 controller has two decisive failures.

FAILURE A — FUNGIBLE REPAIR DEBT

Five local 5% disturbances produced:

approximately 23%
topology churn

while:

maximum scalar repair debt
remained only:
approximately 0.126.

Successful local repairs drove:

quarantine
and:
current disagreement

back down.

Those low current-state values
numerically diluted:

historical structural displacement.

Thus:

MANY
SUCCESSFUL PATCHES

COULD
LEAVE
THE LAST
GLOBALLY VALIDATED
SCAFFOLD

WITHOUT:
EXHAUSTING
THE SCALAR
REPAIR BUDGET.

FAILURE B — REGION-ID-ONLY CERTIFICATE INHERITANCE

H147 false inherited-certificate rate:

LOCAL-5:
0.52%.

LOCAL-10:
0.88%.

MOVING-WOUND:
11.24%.

STACKED:
3.77%.

A certificate can remain:
inside the same region label

while:

the structural relations
that justified the certificate

have changed.

H148 asks:

CAN
REPAIR AUTHORITY
BE
NON-FUNGIBLE

AND:

CAN
CERTIFICATE INHERITANCE
FOLLOW
THE ACTUAL
PROOF DEPENDENCIES?

Additional question:

WHEN
A LOCAL REPAIR BUDGET
IS EXHAUSTED

BUT:
THE DAMAGE
IS STILL
SPATIALLY LOCAL,

CAN
YGGDRASIL
RE-DEVELOP
ONLY
THE AFFECTED REGION

INSTEAD OF:

PATCHING FOREVER

OR:

REBUILDING
THE WHOLE FAMILY?

