CORE ARCHITECTURE

THREE STRUCTURAL MODES

MODE 1 — PATCH

Small accepted-region edits.

Uses:
H147 bounded incremental evidence.

MODE 2 — REGIONAL RE-DEVELOPMENT

A bounded affected region
or:
two-region wound

is rebuilt:
from accumulated relational evidence

without:
using current membership assignments
as hard anchors.

Unaffected family topology:
remains accepted.

MODE 3 — GLOBAL BLASTEMA

H144/H147-style
family-wide de-novo reconstruction

when:
structural damage is diffuse
or:
multiple non-fungible repair dimensions
are exhausted.

The controller must distinguish:

LOCAL REPAIR BUDGET EXHAUSTED

from:

GLOBAL SCAFFOLD INVALID.

NON-FUNGIBLE REPAIR ENVELOPE

The repair state is:

A VECTOR.

No dimension can:
buy authority
from another dimension.

B1 — PATH-LENGTH DISPLACEMENT LEDGER

P =
sum
accepted membership changes
/
family size

since:
the last relevant structural validation.

This is:
a path integral.

If:
one member moves twice

both moves:
consume repair budget.

Successful repair:

does NOT
reduce P.

Primary patch bound:

P <= 0.15.

Robustness:
0.10,
0.15,
0.20,
0.25.

B2 — DISTINCT DISPLACEMENT LEDGER

U =
fraction of distinct members
whose accepted region
has changed

since:
the last relevant validation.

Primary bound:

U <= 0.15.

This prevents:
one oscillating subset

from:
looking identical to
a family-wide moving wound.

B3 — DIFFUSION LEDGER

Cumulative normalized entropy
of:
regions touched by accepted structural change.

Unlike H147's rolling diffusion:

this ledger
does NOT forget
an earlier wound

merely because:
current challenge is local again.

Primary global-diffusion bound:

0.45.

B4 — REGION-SPECIFIC REPAIR LEDGER

For accepted region r:

P_r =
membership-change path length
involving r
/
baseline region size.

Primary regional bound:

0.35.

If:
P_r exceeds 0.35

while:
global diffusion <=0.30,

the preferred handoff is:

REGIONAL RE-DEVELOPMENT,

not:
global blastema.

B5 — FAILED-REPAIR LEDGER

Same H147 semantics:

3 consecutive failed cycles
closes:
patch authority.

B6 — CURRENT SAFETY STATE

Quarantine fraction
and:
current relational disagreement

remain:
action-safety signals.

They DO NOT:
erase
B1..B5.

VALUE RISK

Affected active-value mass:

may:
increase audit priority,
freeze risky action,
or:
accelerate handoff timing.

It may NOT:
increase
any structural repair budget.

PRIMARY PATCH ADMISSIBILITY

Incremental patch is allowed only while:

P <=0.15

AND

U <=0.15

AND

cumulative diffusion <=0.45

AND

every involved P_r <=0.35

AND

quarantine <=25%

AND

single patch <=8% of family

AND

failed repair cycles <3.

No weighted average.

Every bound:
is independently authoritative.

SCOPED HANDOFF

REGIONAL RE-DEVELOPMENT

preferred when:

- patch authority has closed;
- cumulative diffusion <=0.30;
- >=70% of challenged / changed ledger mass
  lies in:
  one region
  or:
  one source-target region pair.

GLOBAL BLASTEMA

preferred when:

- cumulative diffusion >0.45;
- more than two accepted regions each carry
  >=15% of cumulative changed mass;
- regional redevelopment fails twice;
- global quarantine exceeds25%;
- or:
  failed repair cycles >=3 across
  multiple regions.

AMBIGUOUS 0.30..0.45 DIFFUSION ZONE

Freeze:
affected action scope.

Acquire:
one additional structural checkpoint.

Then:

regional
or:
global

according to:
the next cumulative footprint estimate.

REGIONAL RE-DEVELOPMENT

Observed scope:

union of:
the dominant challenged source region
and:
its dominant candidate target region.

During maturation:

only:
that scope
is frozen.

Scratch candidate for scoped members:

argmax:
decayed region-evidence mass.

Promotion requires:

- 4 episodes maturation;
- mean candidate support >=0.85;
- >=90% of scoped members support
  the same candidate assignments
  at:
  two consecutive checkpoints.

On promotion:

- update only scoped memberships;
- count:
  1 scratch-reconstruction unit;
- establish:
  new regional validation baseline;
- reset:
  P_r
  for validated scoped regions;
- subtract:
  the validated scope's contribution
  from:
  global path ledger;
- do NOT reset:
  unrelated region ledgers.

GLOBAL BLASTEMA

Use:
H147 primary realization.

Promotion requires:
6 episodes.

Count:
3 scratch units.

On promotion:

reset:
all structural repair ledgers

to:
the new globally validated baseline.

