SUPPORT WITNESSES

At certificate creation:

choose:
4 deterministic members

from:
the same accepted region.

CONTRAST WITNESSES

Choose:
2 deterministic members

from:
different accepted regions.

Witness selection uses:
accepted topology only.

No latent true label.

WITNESS RELATION SIGNATURE

For each support witness:

expected relation:
SAME REGION.

For each contrast witness:

expected relation:
DIFFERENT REGION.

DEPENDENCY-AWARE INHERITANCE

A certificate may survive:
patch,
regional redevelopment,
or:
global redevelopment

only when:

1.
certificate member's accepted relation
to:
all six witnesses

still matches:
the stored witness-relation signature;

2.
no witness is:
structurally challenged;

3.
certificate member itself
is not:
structurally challenged;

4.
calibration class is unchanged;

5.
ordinary H146 contradiction budget
is not exceeded.

Region numeric ID
may change.

If:
the structural relation graph
is equivalent,

the certificate may:
transfer.

This makes inheritance:

RELABEL-INVARIANT

but:

STRUCTURE-SENSITIVE.

COARSE REGION-ID INHERITANCE COMPARATOR

Use:
H147 inheritance.

Certificate survives when:
region ID appears unchanged
and:
support >=0.90.

This isolates:
the dependency-object contribution.

