PRIMARY ACCEPTANCE SHAPE

H148 is supported if:

- E preserves H147's LOCAL-5 / LOCAL-10 cost advantage over F;
- E hands off in R3 before cumulative path length exceeds25%;
- E materially outperforms H147-SCALAR in R3 final ARI;
- E distinguishes R1 LOCAL-10 from R2 DIFFUSE-10;
- E uses regional redevelopment more often than global blastema in R3;
- E uses global redevelopment in most R2 and R7 worlds;
- R4 moving wound cannot hide behind current local appearance;
- E false inherited-certificate rate remains <1% in every primary structural-damage regime;
- dependency-aware inheritance uses fewer revalidation observations than immediate global invalidation;
- R8 PURE RELABEL retains >=95% of valid certificates without false trust;
- value concentration in R5 changes urgency but does not buy structural authority;
- E uses fewer scratch units than F across local / accumulated-local regimes;
- repair ledgers remain bounded and reset only after the corresponding validation scope is re-established.

FAILURE CONDITIONS

Treat H148 as mixed/negative if:

- path ledgers trigger regional/global redevelopment on ordinary LOCAL-5;
- regional redevelopment is as expensive as global blastema;
- moving wound still evades handoff;
- dependency witnesses fail to reduce false inheritance below1%;
- witness rules invalidate most certificates after harmless local repair;
- PURE RELABEL causes broad certificate loss;
- scoped redevelopment repeatedly reconstructs the wrong region pair;
- non-fungible ledgers create permanent repair lockout after successful validation;
- the controller needs latent damage labels to choose scope.

PRIMARY CONFIRMATION SIZE

400 held-out worlds / regime.

10 regimes.

7 policies.

28,000 policy-regime-worlds.

