OUT-OF-BOX EXTENSION

H148 treats repair history as:

A CONSUMED
STRUCTURAL RESOURCE,

not:
a temporary uncertainty score.

A successful patch can:

reduce current uncertainty

without:

refunding
the structural distance
already traveled.

The experiment also treats:
certificate proof provenance

as:
an executable dependency object.

This is analogous to:

incremental build systems

or:

dependency-aware cache invalidation.

When:
an input assumption changes,

invalidate:
the artifacts that depend on it.

Do not:
invalidate the whole world.

Do not:
reuse artifacts whose inputs changed.

For Yggdrasil:

THE TOPOLOGY
IS A DEPENDENCY GRAPH.

THE CERTIFICATE
IS A CACHED PROOF
WITH EXPLICIT INPUTS.

This may permit:

cheap dormancy,
local repair,
and:
safe memory persistence

to coexist.

